i class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/janos-kadar"><span class="enc-name">János Kádár</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">János Kádár was a Hungarian communist leader who headed the country from 1956 to 1988.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jantar-mantar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jantar-mantar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jantar Mantar</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Jantar Mantar is the name of the five astronomical observatories built by Sawai Jai Singh II of Amber in the 1720s and 1730s at Jaipur, Delhi, Ujjain, Varanasi and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/januarius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/januarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Januarius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Januarius (San Gennaro) was a bishop of Benevento martyred around 305, probably in the persecution of Diocletian.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/january-uprising"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/january-uprising.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">January Uprising</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 1863–1864</span><span class="enc-snip">The January Uprising was a Polish and Lithuanian insurrection against Russian rule, beginning in January 1863 in Congress Poland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/janus-of-cyprus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/janus-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Janus of Cyprus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Janus was king of Cyprus from 1398 to 1432.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/janusz-i-of-warsaw"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/janusz-i-of-warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Janusz I of Warsaw</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Janusz I of Warsaw (c. 1346–1429), also called Janusz the Elder, was a Piast duke who ruled the northern and eastern part of Masovia from 1374.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/janusz-ii-of-plock"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/janusz-ii-of-plock.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Janusz II of Płock</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Janusz II was a Piast duke of Masovia who ruled the Duchy of Płock.</span></a></li></ul>
